 r←Test_Misc_027(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;config;successFlag;msg
⍝ Exercise `PerformConfigChecks`: "CIDER.make" must point to a function.
⍝ A "make" that did not point to a function used to be reported to the caller as valid
⍝ although a message was compiled: because the message is only put on display when the
⍝ check failed, the user never saw it.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 ⍝ "make" is checked as `parent`.`projectSpace`.`make`, so point it at a function that exists
 config←∆GetConfigForChecks'packages_dev'
 config.CIDER.projectSpace←'Cider'
 config.CIDER.make←'Cider.Version'
 (successFlag msg)←##.Cider.PerformConfigChecks config
 →T.PassesIf 1≡successFlag
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg

 config.CIDER.make←'ThisIsNotAFunction'
 (successFlag msg)←##.Cider.PerformConfigChecks config
 →T.PassesIf 0≡successFlag
 →T.PassesIf 0<≢msg

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
